From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] segacd-core-tests

Sega CD / Mega-CD runs on Genesis Plus GX through slot's Mega Drive open
path before any Sega CD platform code exists. The core boots a disc only
through a CD BIOS, but it checks nothing in that file beyond opening it,
so a dummy boot ROM written by the test lets these run on CI: a disc
with no BIOS is refused, the region byte at 0x20b picks bios_CD_U, E or
J, cue/bin, iso and chd discs load at 59.92 fps (PAL 49.70) on the
360x240 Mega Drive canvas, and the core gives slot no SAVE_RAM.

Backup RAM is the new save shape. The core writes it itself, only at
unload, into the save dir slot hands it: Saves/scd_U.brm by default,
Saves/<stem>.brm (the m3u stem for a playlist) with
genesis_plus_gx_system_bram set to per game. A formatted file is written
on the first unload even when the game saved nothing, an unchanged one
is not rewritten, the file is read back at load, and a state does not
carry it. A serialize, reload and unserialize writes it and leaves the
game where it was. With slot's options no RAM cart is mounted.

The core joins every m3u line to the playlist's directory, so an
absolute line fails to load.

With SLOT_SEGACD_BIOS pointing at the US BIOS (crc32 9f6f6276) the real
BIOS boots to its menu, alone and with a synthetic disc, and draws
inside the 320-wide picture. SLOT_SEGACD_DISC times a flush by reload
on an owned disc. Without them those tests print a skip. The synthetic
discs carry no security code: that block is Sega's and is not in this
repository.
